1. `${ github.output_path }}` — NOT a real GitHub context! The GITHUB_OUTPUT env is set by the runner automatically; I should NOT set it in env. Remove that line — GITHUB_OUTPUT is pre-set by the runner. Setting it to a fake context would break it (github.output_path doesn't exist → empty string → appendFileSync(') throws → probe fails... which in my script isn't caught by the decision — it would crash the step → step fails → job fails → needs fails → teammate skipped. BAD — that would wedge everything!).

2. `SELF_CREATED_AT: ${{ github.event.repository.updated_at }}` — wrong semantics (that's the repo's update time, not the run's creation). There's no github.run_created_at context. createdAt fallback only matters when run_number missing — REST always provides run_number, so I can drop SELF_CREATED_AT entirely. Same for the run's created_at: the probe's self run record in the API has created_at, but the tie-break compares suppressor vs self via run_number primarily. Drop SELF_CREATED_AT.

